{"actions":[{"actionCode":null,"actionDate":"2025-12-01","source":"Senate","text":"Received in the Senate.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"H38310","actionDate":"2025-11-21","source":"House floor actions","text":"Motion to reconsider laid on the table Agreed to without objection.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H37100","actionDate":"2025-11-21","source":"House floor actions","text":"On agreeing to the resolution Agreed to by the Yeas and Nays: 285 - 98, 2 Present (Roll no. 305). (text: CR H4883)","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"8000","actionDate":"2025-11-21","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Passed/agreed to in House: On agreeing to the resolution Agreed to by the Yeas and Nays: 285 - 98, 2 Present (Roll no. 305).","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H35000","actionDate":"2025-11-21","source":"House floor actions","text":"The previous question was ordered pursuant to the rule on the concurent resolution and preamble.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H8D000","actionDate":"2025-11-21","source":"House floor actions","text":"DEBATE - The House resumed debate on H. Con. Res. 58.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H8D000","actionDate":"2025-11-21","source":"House floor actions","text":"WORDS TAKEN DOWN - During the course of debate, exception was taken to certain words used and a demand was made to have the words take down. Ms. Salazar asked unanimous consent to withdraw the words, Without Objection, the words were withdrawn.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H8D000","actionDate":"2025-11-21","source":"House floor actions","text":"DEBATE - The House proceeded with one hour of debate on H. Con. Res. 58.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H8D000","actionDate":"2025-11-21","source":"House floor actions","text":"Rule provides for consideration of S.J. Res. 80, H.J. Res. 130, H.J. Res. 131, H. Con. Res. 58, H.R. 1949, H.R. 3109, H.R. 5107 and H.R. 5214. The resolution provides for consideration of S.J. Res. 80, H.J. Res. 130, H.J. Res. 131, H. Con. Res. 58, H.R. 1949, H.R. 3109, H.R. 5107, and H.R. 5214 under a closed rule with one hour of general debate on each measure. The resolution also provides for one motion to recommit on H.J. Res. 130, H.J. Res. 131, H.R. 1949, H.R. 3109, H.R. 5107, and H.R. 5214, and one motion to commit S.J. Res. 80.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H30000","actionDate":"2025-11-21","source":"House floor actions","text":"Considered under the provisions of rule H. Res. 879. (consideration: CR H4883-4890)","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H1L210","actionDate":"2025-11-17","source":"House floor actions","text":"Rules Committee Resolution H. Res. 879 Reported to House. Rule provides for consideration of S.J. Res. 80, H.J. Res. 130, H.J. Res. 131, H. Con. Res. 58, H.R. 1949, H.R. 3109, H.R. 5107 and H.R. 5214. The resolution provides for consideration of S.J. Res. 80, H.J. Res. 130, H.J. Res. 131, H. Con. Res. 58, H.R. 1949, H.R. 3109, H.R. 5107, and H.R. 5214 under a closed rule with one hour of general debate on each measure. The resolution also provides for one motion to recommit on H.J. Res. 130, H.J. Res. 131, H.R. 1949, H.R. 3109, H.R. 5107, and H.R. 5214, and one motion to commit S.J. Res. 80.","type":"Floor"},{"actionCode":"H11100","actionDate":"2025-10-24","source":"House floor actions","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Financial Services.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"H11100","actionDate":"2025-10-24","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Submitted in House","type":"IntroReferral"},{"actionCode":"1025","actionDate":"2025-10-24","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Submitted in House","type":"IntroReferral"}],"congress":119,"congressGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-concurrent-resolution/58","cosponsors":[{"bioguideId":"S001176","fullName":"Rep. Scalise, Steve [R-LA-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-24","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"LA"},{"bioguideId":"H001058","fullName":"Rep. Huizenga, Bill [R-MI-4]","isOriginalCospo